  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Angola Health Assistance Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Angola):  The Angola Health Assistance Project (AHAP) aims to improve health outcomes of vulnerable populations through innovative and sustainable interventions. In FY 2024 AHAP is intended to increase the access of quality health services through  training and supervision. Malaria prevention activities will include: facility and community-level malaria case management, social behavior change, and malaria epidemiological and entomological surveillance strengthening. Health systems strengthening activities will focus on: (1) improving data accuracy, timeliness, completeness, and use of data reported through DHIS2 platform for decision making for malaria and FP/RH programming; and (2) capacity building of National Malaria Control Program (NMCP). AHAP will support ITN distribution campaigns in six PMI focus provinces, along with building NMCP&apos;s capacity to conduct national ITN distribution campaigns to cover Angola&apos;s remaining 12 provinces. AHAP will also support implementation of  activities to increase antenatal care uptake and improve communication between healthcare workers and caregivers. Additionally, AHAP will carry out entomological monitoring, including both insecticide resistance and community-based vector bionomic surveillance. AHAP will also implement the following FP/RH activities: dissemination of existing policies and guidelines on healthy timing and spacing of pregnancy and treatment of gender-based violence; increase use of the Health Network Quality Improvement System monitoring tool by local government entities; increase demand for long-acting FP methods; and continue the FP/RH Digital Campaign for youth. In addition,  AHAP will work to strengthen the ability of healthcare providers to offer high-quality, person-centered FP/RH services. .</narrative>
  </description>
